The original does two linear scans on every call: one through all messages in `GetMesg`, then one through that message's fields. This version replaces both with lookups in tables built once from the constant profile data, so each call becomes two array reads.

- **Same results:** duplicates keep the first match, as the original scans do, so every return value is unchanged.
- **Thread-safe setup:** a function-local static builds the tables, and C++ makes that initialization thread-safe.
- **No mutable-state cache:** the tables are built only from the `const` `mesgs` array, never from global mutable state.
- **Memory:** about 128 KB for the message-number table, plus 512 bytes per message for the field tables.
- **Assumptions:** I couldn't check the header here. The code relies on `Profile::mesgs` being an array whose declared size is visible in this file. It also assumes each message has fewer than 65535 fields, which is true of the profile data.

```cpp
const FIT_UINT16 Profile::GetFieldIndex(const FIT_UINT16 mesgNum, const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    struct Tables
    {
        FIT_UINT16 mesgIdx[65536];
        std::vector<std::array<FIT_UINT16, 256>> fieldIdx;

        Tables()
        {
            const size_t numMesgs = sizeof(Profile::mesgs) / sizeof(Profile::mesgs[0]);
            for (size_t i = 0; i < 65536; i++)
                mesgIdx[i] = FIT_UINT16_INVALID;
            fieldIdx.resize(numMesgs);
            for (size_t m = 0; m < numMesgs; m++)
            {
                const MESG &mesg = Profile::mesgs[m];
                if (mesgIdx[mesg.num] == FIT_UINT16_INVALID)
                    mesgIdx[mesg.num] = (FIT_UINT16)m;

                std::array<FIT_UINT16, 256> &tbl = fieldIdx[m];
                tbl.fill(FIT_UINT16_INVALID);
                for (FIT_UINT16 i = 0; i < mesg.numFields; i++)
                {
                    const FIT_UINT8 fnum = mesg.fields[i].num;
                    if (tbl[fnum] == FIT_UINT16_INVALID)
                        tbl[fnum] = i;
                }
            }
        }
    };

    static const Tables *tables = new Tables();

    const FIT_UINT16 m = tables->mesgIdx[mesgNum];
    if (m == FIT_UINT16_INVALID)
        return FIT_UINT16_INVALID;

    return tables->fieldIdx[m][fieldNum];
}
```

```includes
#include <vector>
#include <array>
#include <cstddef>
```